# R09 — Anytime-valid detection on the fair-coin stream

R09 measures v87 Figure 9 (`fig:anytime`) and the paragraph at `sec:exactness` L243: what happens
to a fixed-horizon sign-CUSUM when the monitoring does not stop at the horizon it was calibrated
for, and what a mixture of betting martingales delivers instead. Three arms — a sign-CUSUM, a
`16 × 3 × 2` mixture martingale (MIX) and an e-process CUSUM (e-CUSUM) — run on the **same**
20 000 fair-coin streams over `[1, 4H]` at seven nominal levels, against a 10-point drift grid on
2 000 drift streams per cell.

**Every qualitative claim of L243 and of the Figure 9 caption holds.** The fixed-horizon CUSUM's
realised false-alarm rate climbs by about a factor of four under continued watching; the mixture
stays at or below `α` at all seven levels; the mixture is the faster arm at `η = 0.10`; e-CUSUM
clears `ARL₀ ≥ 1/α` with a minimum margin of `20.54×`; and the CUSUM peeking rate exceeds the
mixture's at every level, at `22.9`–`68.5` paired standard errors on the same streams. **Three
printed numerals move** under the 128-bit re-keying preamble §S6 requires — `18\% → 20\%`,
`409 → 410`, `539 → 533` — which is a D2 and the subject of §"Known deviations".

**Two things this stream makes legible that the submitted artefacts do not.** Panel C's CUSUM and
MIX curves are **right-censored at the simulation horizon on 65–99% of streams** and are therefore
lower bounds pinned to `4H` rather than average run lengths; and panel B's delay is a **conditional**
mean over the streams that alarmed inside `(τ, H]`, at detection rates running from `5.70%` to
`97.60%`. Neither falsifies anything v87 prints — the panel C caption names e-CUSUM alone, whose
censoring is at most `0.055%` — and both are registered, measured and drawn.

## Execution

```bash
./run_experiment_R09.sh                    # measured 314 s: M1 142 s, calibration 0.4 s, H0 144 s, H1 22 s, 10 workers
./run_experiment_R09.sh --n-jobs 1         # measured 1234 s at one worker; byte-identical artefacts
pytest tests/test_R09_claims.py -v
```

`run_experiment_R09.sh` passes `--control-arms ecusum` **explicitly**, so the certified run produces
the audit-only e-CUSUM control arm. `NUM_CHUNKS` is fixed at `10`, so the chunk decomposition — and
therefore every output — is independent of `--n-jobs`. The script is a single stage: the figure and
the seven macros are computed from the in-memory frames, and those frames are then re-serialised and
their digests compared with the files just written, so the figure is certified to describe the
persisted campaign rather than assumed to.

`run_all.sh` discovers `run_experiment_R09.sh` by sorted enumeration; neither `run_all.sh` nor
`run_tests.sh` is edited by this experiment.

