`data/reference/R09/` still carry the four SHA-256 digests the submitted run recorded.

## The measurement

**Constants, carried verbatim from the witness** and traced to their defining lines: `H = 5000`,
`τ = 2500`, `T_ext = 4H = 20 000`, `δ_CUSUM = 0.1`, seven levels `α ∈ {0.10, 0.07, 0.05, 0.035,
0.025, 0.015, 0.01}`, ten drifts `η ∈ {0.02 … 0.20}`, `N_CAL = 50 000`, `N_NULL = 20 000`,
`N_ALT = 2 000`, `NUM_CHUNKS = 10`. The mixture is `96 = 16` start times `× 3` betting fractions
`× 2` sides at uniform weight `1/96`.

**Three arms and three different guarantees.**

| arm      | alarm rule                   | guarantee             | threshold             |
| -------- | ---------------------------- | --------------------- | --------------------- |
| `CUSUM`  | `max(S⁺, S⁻) ≥ λ*`           | fixed horizon `[1,H]` | calibrated on `N_CAL` |
| `MIX`    | `logsumexp(logM) ≥ −log α`   | Ville, time-uniform   | `1/α`, exact          |
| `eCUSUM` | `max(logM⁺, logM⁻) ≥ −log α` | `ARL₀` only           | `1/α`, exact          |

**Three stopping protocols**, and the third is the one v87 does not describe: `nominal` is
`{fa ≤ H}`, `peeking` is `{fa ≤ 4H}`, and `extended` is the **crossing state at exactly `t = 4H`**,
not a cumulative probability. Panel A plots all three. `peeking` dominates the other two **by
construction** — `{fa ≤ H}` and `{cross at 4H}` are both subsets of `{fa ≤ 4H}` — which is why the
two `…PeekingFprMax` macros are always the peeking bar.

**Everything is paired.** Every entropy key carries a role and an index and never a process
parameter, so the same key serves every grid point: the three arms read the same `y_t` inside a
chunk, and the H1 campaign draws one uniform block per chunk **before** the `η` loop, so two drifts
consume the identical uniform stream and differ only where the threshold moves. Every between-arm
comparison at fixed `(α, η)`, and every comparison across `η` and across `α`, is paired by
construction. No pooled interval is published; the one paired comparison control C4 reads ships with
its measured Kish design effect.

